  "query_preview": "..\n\nLow pressure will exit east as an upper ridge tracks over the\nregion for Tuesday into Wednesday. This will lead generally dry\nweather conditions and seasonable temperatures. Lows each morning\nwill range in the upper 20s to low 30s while highs push into the\nupper 40s to low 50s.\n\nThe upper ridge will slide east of the Northern Rockies and into\nthe Plains while the next shortwave tracks along the MT northern\nborder with Canada late in the week. This may bring enough dynamic\nlift support for an isolated shower to NE Montana by Friday night\nor Saturday, but ensemble QPF amounts look light at this time. For\nnow, NBM is mainly placing silent pops over the area.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was left untouched for this forecast cycle as it captured the\noverall seasonable temperatures and dry weather well for the next\nseveral days. Confidence decreases late in the week with\nprecipitation chances as the next system approaches given the\nmarginal thermal profiles and overall light nature of the expected\ntotal QPF if it occurs.",
